    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// The lookup node above replaces our data with whatever row it found (or\n// {} via Always Output Data if nothing matched, or an {error: ...} shaped\n// item if the sheet is missing a filtered-on column) -- recover the real\n// message data (and its binary attachments) from before the lookup, and\n// just carry forward whether a real row was found.\n//\n// 'row_number' (not 'id') is the found-signal: it's a field n8n's Sheets\n// node always attaches to every real matched row, regardless of which\n// actual columns that row has -- unlike 'id', which only exists on rows\n// logged by this dedup feature itself. Matching is done on timestamp +\n// fromEmail + toEmail + subject (see the lookup node) specifically because\n// those columns already exist on every row ever logged, old and new, so\n// messages logged before this feature existed are still correctly\n// recognized as already-logged instead of silently re-duplicated.\nconst lookupResult = $input.first().json;\nconst original = $('Normalize | Extract Clean Reply Text2').item;\nreturn [{\n  json: { ...original.json, _alreadyLogged: !!(lookupResult && lookupResult.row_number !== undefined) },\n  binary: original.binary\n}];"
      },
